; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/ds4-stream-sanity.fk
;
; ds4-stream-sanity-band — eight claims about the reading that was missing while
; 107 harness gates and 54 suite gates stood green over a stream saying
; " the name, the<|place_holder_mm_span_0155|> detection device detection device".
; Verdict 255 when every one crosses.
;
; run: ./fkwu --src form/form-stdlib/tests/ds4-stream-sanity-band.fk   ; -> 255
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; APORON — THE DECLARED RADIUS. Read this before believing the number.
;
; WHAT THIS BAND PROVES
;   That three cheap readings of an emitted token stream — reserved-block
;   emission, single-id multiplicity, alternating-run length — separate the two
;   streams this body actually produced on 2026-08-04 from the SAME commit on two
;   different weight files, and separate a third recorded stream that only one of
;   the three can see. It proves the readings are INDEPENDENT and that the guard
;   for short streams does not silence the reserved reading.
;
; WHAT IT DOES NOT PROVE
;   * NOT that the answer is true. " Jupiter is a moon of Mars" passes every
;     reading here. Truth is ~/models/ds4-engine/ds4's to answer, not this cell's.
;   * NOT that the stream matches ds4 token for token. That check exists and is a
;     change-detector for kernel work (receipts/2026-08-01-the-model-is-useful.md);
;     this one is a floor beneath it that needs no reference process.
;   * NOT the arithmetic. Every kernel could be right and this still red, because
;     the lane can be open on the wrong file — which is exactly what happened.
;   * NOT a live run. The three streams are RECORDED, dated, and attributable. The
;     door applies the same predicate to a live stream; this band proves the
;     predicate, and the two must not be confused.
;
; A gate reading "the stream is 33 tokens long and every id is in the vocabulary"
; would have passed the reaped specimen's answer without a flicker. Claim 16 exists
; because of that: it hands the band a DELIBERATELY WEAKENED predicate — the
; reserved reading alone, the symptom a reader notices first — and demands it go
; blind on a stream the full predicate catches.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
;   bit   1  THE RESERVED BLOCK IS READ: the mainline stream carries 0 ids at or
;            above 128000; the reaped specimen's carries 2. The block's edges are
;            the tokenizer's own (claim 128).
;   bit   2  MULTIPLICITY IS READ: mainline's most frequent id appears 2 times in
;            33 and does not trip; the specimen's appears 9 and does.
;   bit   4  THE ALTERNATING RUN IS READ: mainline's longest a·b·a·b run is 2 and
;            does not trip; the specimen's is 7 and does.
;   bit   8  THE PREDICATE SEPARATES THE TWO WEIGHT FILES: dss-degenerate? is 0 on
;            the mainline stream and 1 on the reaped specimen's — same commit, same
;            prompt, same day, different file.
;   bit  16  THE FALSIFIER CAN FAIL: the reserved reading ALONE is blind to the
;            2026-07-30 stream (0), which the full predicate refuses (1). A gate
;            built on the placeholder marker alone would have shipped.
;   bit  32  THE READINGS ARE INDEPENDENT: trip counts are 0 for mainline, exactly
;            1 for the 2026-07-30 stream, and all 3 for the reaped specimen. Three
;            distinct answers, so no reading is a restatement of another.
;   bit  64  SHORT STREAMS DO NOT FALSE-ALARM, AND ARE NOT EXEMPT: one ordinary
;            token reads healthy (the repetition guard holds), one reserved token
;            reads degenerate (the guard does not reach the reserved reading).
;   bit 128  THE BLOCK IS EXACTLY 1280 SLOTS WIDE AND ITS FLOOR IS WITNESSED:
;            129280 - 128000 = 1280, and 127999 — the last ordinary id, 屋檐 — is
;            below the floor by exactly one.

(do
    (defn dsb-score (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))
    (defn ds4-stream-sanity-band ()
        (do
    (let ml (dss-mainline-stream))
    (let rp (dss-reap25-stream))
    (let s0 (dss-0730-stream))

    (let c0 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-reserved-count ml) 0)
                           (eq (dss-reserved-count rp) 2) 0) 1))

    (let c1 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-max-mult ml) 2)
                           (if (eq (dss-mult-trip? ml) 0)
                               (if (eq (dss-max-mult rp) 9)
                                   (eq (dss-mult-trip? rp) 1) 0) 0) 0) 2))

    (let c2 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-longest-two-cycle ml) 2)
                           (if (eq (dss-cycle-trip? ml) 0)
                               (if (eq (dss-longest-two-cycle rp) 7)
                                   (eq (dss-cycle-trip? rp) 1) 0) 0) 0) 4))

    (let c3 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-degenerate? ml) 0)
                           (eq (dss-degenerate? rp) 1) 0) 8))

    (let c4 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-reserved-trip? s0) 0)
                           (eq (dss-degenerate? s0) 1) 0) 16))

    (let c5 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-trip-count ml) 0)
                           (if (eq (dss-trip-count s0) 1)
                               (eq (dss-trip-count rp) 3) 0) 0) 32))

    (let c6 (dsb-score (if (eq (dss-degenerate? (dss-one-ordinary)) 0)
                           (eq (dss-degenerate? (dss-one-reserved)) 1) 0) 64))

    (let c7 (dsb-score (if (eq (sub (dss-vocab-size) (dss-reserved-floor)) 1280)
                           (eq (sub (dss-reserved-floor) (dss-last-ordinary)) 1) 0) 128))

    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 (add c3 (add c4 (add c5 (add c6 c7)))))))))
    (ds4-stream-sanity-band))
